          <!-- ───────────────────────────────────────── [12] Who it's for -->
          <section class="who" aria-labelledby="who-title" data-who>
            <div class="who__head">
              <p class="tag">[12] Who it's for</p>
              <h2 id="who-title" class="h2" data-reveal>For whoever is directing the agents.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="who__list">
              <ul class="acc">
                <li class="acc__item is-open">
                  <h3><button class="acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="acc-0" id="acc-0-btn">Solo developers<i class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></i></button></h3>
                  <div class="acc__panel" id="acc-0" role="region" aria-labelledby="acc-0-btn"><div><p>Plan in one thread, fan the pieces out to Claude Code and Codex in separate worktrees, or fork a checkpoint to compare two models side by side.</p></div></div>
                </li>
                <li class="acc__item">
                  <h3><button class="acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-6" id="acc-6-btn">Engineers who answer for what ships<i class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></i></button></h3>
                  <div class="acc__panel" id="acc-6" role="region" aria-labelledby="acc-6-btn"><div><p>Read an agent’s change with the same language servers and code index it used, see it drawn on a canvas, and merge knowing what it does.</p></div></div>
                </li>
                <li class="acc__item">
                  <h3><button class="acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-1" id="acc-1-btn">Reviewers<i class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></i></button></h3>
                  <div class="acc__panel" id="acc-1" role="region" aria-labelledby="acc-1-btn"><div><p>Every pull request a task produced, and the wiki change that documents them, sit in one change group, so the code and its docs are read side by side and merge together.</p></div></div>
                </li>
                <li class="acc__item">
                  <h3><button class="acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-2" id="acc-2-btn">Maintainers<i class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></i></button></h3>
                  <div class="acc__panel" id="acc-2" role="region" aria-labelledby="acc-2-btn"><div><p>Keep conventions and the decisions behind the code in a wiki of linked Markdown in git that every agent reads. Agent edits collect in a pull request, and the wiki changes only when you merge.</p></div></div>
                </li>
                <li class="acc__item">
                  <h3><button class="acc__btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="acc-5" id="acc-5-btn">Teams with skills of their own<i class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></i></button></h3>
                  <div class="acc__panel" id="acc-5" role="region" aria-labelledby="acc-5-btn"><div><p>Keep the skills your team already wrote where your agents load them. Run one from the composer with <code>$</code>, under any agent, and it can read your wiki, draw a canvas and search your code through Astrolabe’s tools.</p></div></div>
                </li>
              </ul>
            </div>
          </section>
